        "text_sha256": "a3d458e1bd1eda066018d8db2dd5537c9e742f02f68401457c01553e77f57403",
        "word_count": 3
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000040",
        "block_index": 40,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h4",
        "text": "What week does an IVF transfer happen?",
        "text_sha256": "7e79b933772485fb581e55843e27df2ee5e59a75b94553a12997cddfc6910c45",
        "word_count": 7
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000041",
        "block_index": 41,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "IVF transfers typically happen during the second week of pregnancy . You can add two weeks to the date of your transfer to find out how many weeks pregnant you are.",
        "text_sha256": "1525f08ae8be5622d721c7ccaea9d5918985bf70f8a8bf8b15ea27d1b6c06f69",
        "word_count": 31
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000042",
        "block_index": 42,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h4",
        "text": "How many weeks pregnant are you after a five-day embryo transfer?",
        "text_sha256": "32e422aa8898ff5718af66d01ef2a202f48f748e3d49d76f717bf0cdb0ca8390",
        "word_count": 11
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000043",
        "block_index": 43,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "If your embryo transfer is a success, you would be 2 weeks and 5 days pregnant on the day of your transfer.",
        "text_sha256": "57cda18ab9b0ce2c2fff56ae80ace02fc8d2e4a664ceb26a110148e0e8337667",
        "word_count": 22
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000044",
        "block_index": 44,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h4",
        "text": "Is your due date different with IVF?",
        "text_sha256": "18c2b2289bd1dc99ee32655ba4b64bf72ea78a84194a4659e4f29c5cb3aba264",
        "word_count": 7
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000045",
        "block_index": 45,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Your IVF pregnancy is still the same length as a natural pregnancy, but you can calculate your due date based on your transfer date, rather than on the first day of your last period or on your conception date.",
        "text_sha256": "1385bbf5248534fc5e85bbc60457377024bef2acaffb362cf570a091be65fd7a",
        "word_count": 39
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000046",
        "block_index": 46,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h4",
        "text": "How accurate is your due date with IVF?",
        "text_sha256": "e8746fd1b3e881c456e0d4527f62c7a3837d3f9c1efd34a8fce52babca00cd46",
        "word_count": 8
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000047",
        "block_index": 47,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "An IVF due date is as accurate as any other estimated due date, but keep in mind that only 4 percent of babies are born on their actual due dates.",
        "text_sha256": "2042bd6edc2a749db312b57c57b39c225ec62733093551758f853123bb796a26",
        "word_count": 30
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000048",
        "block_index": 48,
        "block_type": "blockquote",
        "tag": "blockquote",
